# The timing record's artifact upload, as an installable patch (#529)

`CONTRIBUTING.md` ENV-03 says every CI workflow whose jobs this repository
defines uploads `.timings/` — the run's own timing record — as an artifact with
90-day retention.  The seven workflow changes that do it are here as a patch
rather than in the history, because the connection that pushed this work may not
update a file under `.github/workflows/`: GitHub refuses the ref with

    refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow
    `.github/workflows/coble-gamma-co-2-incidence-rows.yml` without `workflows`
    permission

which is a permission of the GitHub App behind the connection, not something a
commit can carry.  Everything else of #529 is on `main` and needs nothing from
this file.

**Install (one command, from the repository root):**

```sh
git apply results/issue529-timing-record-workflows.patch
```

Then commit the seven modified workflows.  They are:

| workflow | what the patch adds |
| --- | --- |
| `coble-gamma-co-2-incidence-rows.yml` | the upload step, at the end of the job |
| `coble-kernel-plane-rows.yml` | the upload step, at the end of the job |
| `enriques-polarization-rows.yml` | the upload step, at the end of the job |
| `research-388-acceptance.yml` | the upload step, at the end of the job |
| `research-564-sage-image.yml` | the upload step, at the end of the job |
| `readme.yml` | the upload step, before the file's top-level `concurrency:` |
| `isotropic-reduction-image-tests.yml` | replaces the `tests/.report/` upload with `.timings/`: `tests/.report/` is what the next run overwrites, `.timings/` is the record |

`development.yml` and `ambient.yml` are not in the patch and cannot be: their
jobs are `uses:` calls to `ai-review-ci`'s reusable `_qc.yml`, which owns every
step and takes no artifact path, so their run's record is that workflow's to
upload.  ENV-03 says so.

The patch is the diff of those seven files between `da0fa12` (the merge this
work landed on) and the commit that carried them before this file replaced it;
`git apply --check` passes against that tree.
diff --git a/.github/workflows/coble-gamma-co-2-incidence-rows.yml b/.github/workflows/coble-gamma-co-2-incidence-rows.yml
index 547c959..9e718dd 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/coble-gamma-co-2-incidence-rows.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/coble-gamma-co-2-incidence-rows.yml
@@ -58,3 +58,14 @@ jobs:
           "$sage_python" tests/coble_gamma_co_2_incidence_rows.py \
             --cap "$COBLE_CALL_CAP" --budget "$COBLE_ROW_BUDGET"
         shell: bash
+      # The run's own timing record (CONTRIBUTING.md ENV-03): the test run's
+      # report log and JUnit file as the run's plugin copied them into
+      # .timings/, and the stage records the library appended as it computed.
+      - name: Keep the run's timing record
+        if: always()
+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
+        with:
+          name: timings-${{ github.job }}-${{ github.sha }}
+          path: .timings/
+          retention-days: 90
+          if-no-files-found: warn
